## 1. Add the dev tools to the workspace image

The overlay image (`debian:bookworm-slim` + `fuse-overlayfs util-linux procps curl ca-certificates git`) needs, for this test only:

- `python3`, `python3-venv`, `pipx`: the Coder `jupyterlab` module installs JupyterLab with `pipx` if it is not already there. (Its other branch, `uv`, needs an existing `~/.venv`; stick to `pipx`.)
- `node`: compiles the TypeScript half of the extension. `jlpm` (yarn) ships with JupyterLab.
- `ws-publish` and `ws-base` on the `PATH` (you already have these in `/opt/ws`).

```dockerfile
FROM debian:bookworm-slim
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
      fuse-overlayfs util-linux procps curl ca-certificates git \
      python3 python3-venv pipx \
 && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/* \
 && useradd -u 1000 -m -s /bin/bash coder
COPY --from=node:20-bookworm-slim /usr/local/bin/node /usr/local/bin/node
# ws-publish (Go binary) and ws-base, if not mounted from a ConfigMap
COPY ws-publish ws-base /opt/ws/
ENV PATH=/opt/ws:/home/coder/.local/bin:$PATH
USER 1000
WORKDIR /home/coder
```

Network: at workspace start the module runs `pipx install jupyterlab` (PyPI), and step 7 runs `pip install -e` (PyPI, for `hatchling`) and `jlpm install` (npm registry). If the workspace has no internet, point them at your mirrors in the pod env: `PIP_INDEX_URL=https://…`, `YARN_NPM_REGISTRY_SERVER=https://…`.

