## 3. Check the workspace

Open a terminal in the workspace (Coder web terminal, or `coder ssh <workspace>`):

```bash
command -v ws-publish ws-base git node pipx
cat /data/overlay/.base_commit_sha
ls /data/overlay/upper | head
echo "remote=$GITLAB_REMOTE user=$WS_USER token_set=$([ -n "$GITLAB_TOKEN" ] && echo yes || echo NO)"

# the module's JupyterLab: installed by pipx and running
ls ~/.local/bin/jupyter-lab
pgrep -af 'jupyter-lab --no-browser'
tail -5 /tmp/jupyterlab.log
```

All five commands found, a base SHA, `token_set=yes`, and one `jupyter-lab --no-browser …` process. If JupyterLab is not there yet, the module is still installing it: wait and look at `/tmp/jupyterlab.log`.

Open JupyterLab once from the Coder dashboard (the **JupyterLab** app) to confirm it loads.

