## 9. The edit loop

Put this in `~/.bashrc` (or run it in each terminal) so `jlpm` and `jupyter` point at the module's environment:

```bash
export PATH="$(pipx environment --value PIPX_LOCAL_VENVS)/jupyterlab/bin:$PATH"
```

| You changed | Do |
| --- | --- |
| `src/index.ts` (labels, dialogs, icons, menu order) | `cd /home/coder/dev/ws_actions && jlpm build`, then reload the browser tab |
| `schema/plugin.json` (toolbar position, top menu) | `jlpm build`, reload; if nothing changes, `restart-jupyter.sh` then reload |
| `ws_actions/handlers.py` (which command runs, validation, timeouts) | `/home/coder/dev/scripts/restart-jupyter.sh`, reload |
| `style/index.css` | `jlpm build`, reload |

Built-in icons you can use instead of the custom one: `import { <name> } from '@jupyterlab/ui-components'`. Common ones: `shareIcon`, `moveUpIcon`, `refreshIcon`, `undoIcon`, `redoIcon`, `listIcon`, `runIcon`, `saveIcon`, `downloadIcon`, `buildIcon`, `bugIcon`, `settingsIcon`, `checkIcon`, `closeIcon`.

**After a workspace restart** there is nothing to redo. `/home/coder` is on the PVC, so the module finds the `pipx` JupyterLab in `~/.local` (it skips the install, or `pipx` says "already installed"), starts it, and the editable install, the frontend link and the server enable are all still there. Only run `dev-setup.sh` again if you delete `~/.local/share/pipx` or run `pipx upgrade jupyterlab` / `pipx reinstall jupyterlab`.

