## 10. When you are happy: build the wheel and bake it into the image

### 10.1 Build the wheel (in the workspace)

```bash
cd /home/coder/dev/ws_actions
export PATH="$(pipx environment --value PIPX_LOCAL_VENVS)/jupyterlab/bin:$PATH"
jlpm build:prod
pipx runpip jupyterlab install -q build
python -m build --wheel --no-isolation --outdir dist
ls dist/          # ws_actions-0.1.0-py3-none-any.whl
```

Commit `/home/coder/dev/ws_actions` to your own repo (without `node_modules/`, `lib/`, `ws_actions/labextension/`, `dist/`) so the image build can produce the wheel in CI.

### 10.2 Production image: JupyterLab and the wheel pre-installed

```dockerfile
# Build the extension wheel. Context: the folder that contains ws_actions/
FROM python:3.12-bookworm AS build
COPY --from=node:20-bookworm-slim /usr/local/bin/node /usr/local/bin/node
RUN pip install --no-cache-dir "jupyterlab>=4.2,<5" build hatchling
WORKDIR /src
COPY ws_actions/ ./
RUN jlpm install && jlpm build:prod && python -m build --wheel --no-isolation --outdir /dist

FROM debian:bookworm-slim
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
      fuse-overlayfs util-linux procps curl ca-certificates git python3 python3-venv \
 && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/* \
 && useradd -u 1000 -m -s /bin/bash coder
# One environment for JupyterLab and the extension (Debian's system pip refuses installs: PEP 668).
COPY --from=build /dist/*.whl /tmp/
RUN python3 -m venv /opt/jupyter \
 && /opt/jupyter/bin/pip install --no-cache-dir "jupyterlab>=4.2,<5" /tmp/*.whl \
 && rm /tmp/*.whl
COPY ws-publish ws-base /opt/ws/
ENV PATH=/opt/ws:/opt/jupyter/bin:$PATH
USER 1000
WORKDIR /home/coder
```

No node, no pipx in the final image. The module finds `jupyter-lab` on the `PATH`, skips its install and starts it; the extension is already there (the wheel enables its server half by itself).

Check the image:

```bash
docker run --rm <image> sh -c 'command -v jupyter-lab; jupyter labextension list; jupyter server extension list'
# /opt/jupyter/bin/jupyter-lab, "ws-actions ... enabled OK", "ws_actions enabled ... OK"
```

### 10.3 Template

Keep the `module "jupyterlab"` block (with its `config`) and the `GITLAB_*`, `WS_USER`, `SCRATCH_ROOT` env from [step 2](#2-add-the-module-and-the-environment-to-the-template) unchanged; only the image changes.

Existing workspaces still have the dev JupyterLab in `~/.local/share/pipx/venvs/jupyterlab` on their PVC. It is harmless as long as `/opt/jupyter/bin` comes before `~/.local/bin` on the `PATH` (the production image above does not add `~/.local/bin` at all); to clean up: `pipx uninstall jupyterlab && rm -rf ~/dev`.

